==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
The biggest threat in this level is Zapy, who can be dangerous for much the same reasons as [[Capy|before she became a Zombie]]. Zapy's faster attack rate can make things problematic, as can the Cat limit in this outbreak. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Sifu Cat]] is optimal, as a high enough level Sifu can survive one hit from Zapy. However, deploying other meatshields without necessarily spamming them is recommended, as this stage contains not just multiple Zapies but also Star Pengs. It also contains Shibalien and Ginger Snache, though neither of these peons is a threat in this level. Additionally, both Zapy and Star Peng can warp any meatshields away, assuming that they survive, so multiple meatshields (preferably [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Erasers]] and Sifu) are necessary to properly stall them.

As for attackers, any decent attackers work here. [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] can deal decent damage to both Star Peng and Zapy, in addition to a chance to slow Zapy and kill her permanently.

Notably, Star Peng is magnified to 200% in this stage. As such, with enough [[Treasure]]s, it can only threaten anything by warping it away before it inevitably crumbles. As for the [[Cat Cannon]], the [[Ototo Corps|Holy Blast]] is the best option. It deals big damage to the Zapies, freezes them, and can prevent them from reviving if it gets the final hit on any of them.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The strategy for this stage is much simpler than the strategy from the first stage, as this stage contins no Zapy, but buffed Star Pengs and Shy Boys, which can easily be dealt with using [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], as these enemies get anihilated when they can't deal damage. The problem will only arise once Ribbo starts warping your units, causing the Star Pengs to unfreeze and deal damage to your warp inmmune or oncoming units. You can deal with this by using wave attacks or using high damage attackers to kill the Ribbos before the Star Pengs arrive.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
This stage is also quite simple; however, players may risk losing to the initial Zir Zeal as it burrows to their base and quickly destroys it. It is thus recommended to use a fast, disposable unit to force it to burrow, like [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] or [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]], before sending out [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] and an anti-Zombie nuker, like [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]. Thanks to the minimal peon spam, reasonably fast attackers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] can dispose of Gardeneel Bros. quickly before Spacefish Jones spawns. Be sure to use strong units to dispatch of the Shy Boy before it pushes too hard, with [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] being excellent options for it; the latter is also great for chunking Spacefish Jones' health.

Alternatively, you can cheese the stage by using two Medium and one Small money-up combos and a [[Battle Items#Rich Cat|Rich Cat]] power-up. At around 1,500 cents, spawn [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] to make the zombies burrow, then spawn [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] (requires Explosion [[Talents|Talent]]). You should destroy the base just before Spacefish Jones kills Bahamut. (If he is level 30, you will want to spawn [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] to deal just a little bit more damage to the enemy base, since at Lv.30, Bahamut takes five hits to destroy the base instead of four.)

